          "slug": "theorem-collider_energy_is_below_the_planck_scale",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED: the Planck energy is 897713235294117 times the LHC's collision energy, exactly — 13600 GeV divides 1.220890 x 10^19 GeV 897713235294117 times with 8800 GeV left over. String theory's characteristic scale is fifteen orders of magnitude past the most energetic instrument ever built."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(13600 * 897713235294117 + 8800 = 12208900000000000000) ∧ (8800 < 13600)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem collider_energy_is_below_the_planck_scale : (13600 * 897713235294117 + 8800 = 12208900000000000000) ∧ (8800 < 13600) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
