              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(1616255 * 3217314099569684239182554733009 + 538705 = 52 * 10 ^ 35) ∧ (538705 < 1616255)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem newtonian_gravity_is_verified_far_above_the_planck_length : (1616255 * 3217314099569684239182554733009 + 538705 = 52 * 10 ^ 35) ∧ (538705 < 1616255) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-the_proton_outlives_the_universe_many_times_over",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED: the proton's lifetime bound exceeds the age of the universe 1739130434782608695652173 times over — 2.4 x 10^34 years against 1.38 x 10^10, with a remainder of 12600000000 years. Grand unification predicted a decay; twenty-four orders of magnitude of waiting have not seen one."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(138 * 10 ^ 8 * 1739130434782608695652173 + 12600000000 = 24 * 10 ^ 33) ∧ (12600000000 < 138 * 10 ^ 8)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem the_proton_outlives_the_universe_many_times_over : (138 * 10 ^ 8 * 1739130434782608695652173 + 12600000000 = 24 * 10 ^ 33) ∧ (12600000000 < 138 * 10 ^ 8) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-one_probe_reached_the_planck_scale_and_found_nothing",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "CLAIMED: of the six searches quoted here exactly one has reached the Planck scale — photon timing across a gamma-ray burst, which bounded linear quantum-gravity dispersion above 1.2 Planck energies and saw no dispersion. The collider is short of the scale and the torsion balance is above it; the one instrument that arrived returned null."
                }
              ]
            },
